{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>She shall not go out as the slaves go out.</b> It is not fitting for a proper person to acquire a Hebrew woman as a maidservant against her will. Rather, his purchase must be to take her as a wife for himself or for his son, and the money of her sale must be given as kiddushin to her father, who is entitled to it, in accordance with what is stated in their received tradition, of blessed memory (Ketuvot 46b)."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:26:38.281163422Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}